1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,630
Do you prefer to watch TV or listen to the radio?
你喜欢看电视还是听广播？

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:17,080
There was a time when some people thought moving pictures beamed live into our houses would spell the end of tuning in to the radio for entertainment and information.
曾几何时，一些人认为，实时传输到家中的动态影像会终结人们通过收听广播获取娱乐和信息的方式。

3
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:20,390
But radio survived and flourished.
但广播不仅存活了下来，还愈发繁荣。

4
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:30,800
And now, despite the growth in sophisticated smartphones offering high-definition pictures, the popularity of podcasts is booming.
如今，尽管功能先进、能提供高清画质的智能手机日益普及，播客的受欢迎程度却在急剧上升。

5
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:48,810
Perhaps the growth in podcasting is not surprising – it offers a digital audio file that can be downloaded and stored for listening at any time. It can also be streamed from the internet and played on a computer or MP3 player.
播客的兴起或许并不令人意外——它提供的是一种数字音频文件，可下载存储后随时收听，也能通过互联网流媒体播放，在电脑或MP3播放器上使用。

6
00:00:48,810 --> 00:01:04,010
And it’s not just broadcasters, like the BBC, who are producing podcasts: now commercial broadcasters, individuals and companies with no connection to broadcasting are making them.
而且，制作播客的并非只有BBC这样的广播机构：如今，商业广播公司、个人以及与广播行业毫无关联的企业都在涉足这一领域。

7
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:11,710
In fact, anyone with something to say, and a few pounds to spend on the equipment, can get involved.
事实上，只要有话想说，再花几英镑购置设备，任何人都能参与其中。

8
00:01:11,710 --> 00:01:17,710
But where did this trend for making portable audio programmes begin?
但这种便携式音频节目的潮流是从何而起的呢？

9
00:01:17,710 --> 00:01:27,380
Journalist Ben Hammersley told the BBC that “two changes transformed the market – one cultural and one technical.”
记者本·哈默斯利向英国广播公司表示：“两项变革改变了这个市场——一项是文化层面的，另一项是技术层面的。”

10
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:39,340
Apple launched the iPhone podcast app, recording and editing equipment became cheaper, and 4G mobile phone connections and Wi-Fi became widespread.
苹果公司推出了iPhone播客应用，录音和编辑设备变得更加廉价，4G移动网络和无线网络也得到了广泛普及。

11
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:45,580
Technological development has driven many changes in our media consumption habits.
技术发展推动了我们媒体消费习惯的诸多改变。

12
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:52,860
But however good the tech may be, there still needs to be something worth watching or listening to.
但无论技术多么先进，仍需要有值得观看或收听的内容。

13
00:01:52,860 --> 00:02:04,460
The BBC’s Jamie Robertson writes that for podcasts, Serial - a piece of non-fiction investigative journalism – captured people’s imagination.
英国广播公司的杰米·罗伯逊写道，播客节目《连环》（Serial）——一档非虚构调查类新闻节目——激发了人们的兴趣。

14
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:09,350
It was a piece of high-quality audio with a gripping story.
这档音频节目质量上乘，故事扣人心弦。

15
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:17,310
To date, the first and second seasons of the show have had more than 340 million downloads.
截至目前，该节目的第一、二季下载量已超过3.4亿次。

16
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:24,710
Advertisers soon realised the money-making potential of this and other successful podcasts.
广告商们很快就意识到了这档节目以及其他成功播客的盈利潜力。

17
00:02:24,710 --> 00:02:34,100
Now there are podcasts about anything and everything - even the educational content that BBC Learning English offers!
如今，播客的内容无所不包——甚至包括BBC英语教学提供的教育类内容！

18
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:40,360
And these aural treats are available on a wide range of platforms.
这些听觉盛宴可在众多平台上获取。

19
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:47,140
Audiences are very specific, which can help advertisers target what they want to promote.
播客的受众群体非常精准，这有助于广告商针对性地推广产品。

20
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:56,300
And if there isn’t a podcast to suit your interests, you can now easily make and distribute them - and become your very own broadcaster.
而且，如果你找不到感兴趣的播客，现在也能轻松制作并发布——成为自己专属的广播人。
